The Last Signal
Project: an alien sci-fi movie poster featuring a strange unreal, extraterrestrial world.
First image: IMG.png
Second Image: IMG.png

AI immage prompt for first immage:
Create a surreal science-fiction movie poster titled “THE LAST SIGNAL.” Show an extremely strange alien world with a giant black and violet planet, a colossal faceless alien creature with asymmetrical limbs and glowing eyes, floating stone structures, twisted towers, and strange floating organisms. Use acid-green and violet lighting,
deep black shadows, swirling particles, and dramatic contrast. Make the world feel mysterious, unsettling, and completely alien, with unusual shapes, curved and jagged lines, and a sense of impossible depth. Use a cinematic poster composition.

AI immage prompt for second immage:
Create a surreal science-fiction movie poster titled “THE LAST SIGNAL.” Keep the same strange alien world, giant black and violet planet, colossal faceless alien creature with asymmetrical limbs and glowing eyes, floating stone structures, twisted towers, and strange floating organisms. Keep the same composition, lighting, colors, and placement of the main elements. Change only the surface textures: make the alien creature rough, cracked, porous, and ancient-looking instead of smooth and polished. Add rough textures to the floating stone structures as well. 
Use acid-green and violet lighting, deep black shadows, swirling particles, and dramatic contrast. Make the world feel more ancient, hostile, and unsettling while keeping the overall design recognizable as the same poster.

Vocab List
1. Lines-The soft curved lines make the picture look calmer and less harsh.
2. Shape-The unusual shapes make the alien world look fake and unrealistic.
3. Texture-The smooth texture looks nicer while the rough cracked texture looks messy and broken.
4. Volume-The different sizes make the alien and planet look like they take up real space.
5. Contrast-The bright green and violet colors stand out against the dark background.

Reflection:I think the curved lines make the picture look softer and less harsh. The bright green and violet colors stand out against the dark background and bring attention to different parts of the picture. The alien and the planet also look like they take up real space because of their different sizes. I like the second picture better because I feel like it makes the aliens look scarier. I think it would catch people’s attention more than the first picture. The first picture looks smooth and more minimalistic but the second one looks rough and cracked. It looks broken and not well taken care of. 
This makes the alien world feel more scary and abandoned. The AI made the pictures different from what I expected. When I think of aliens I usually think of the ones I see in movies. These aliens looked completely different from what I imagined. I also expected the colors to be more neon and vibrant but they looked darker than I thought they would. Changing the texture made a big difference in the mood. The rough and cracked texture made the second picture look scarier and more like something you might see online. The smooth texture was different from what I usually see in alien pictures.
Overall I prefer the second picture because it looks more intense and catches my attention more.
